  "result": "Perfect! All 145 tests pass. I've successfully implemented the payments system:\n\n**Created `src/payments.js` with two functions:**\n\n1. **recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })**\n   - Records a payment on an invoice\n   - Creates `invoice.payments` array if missing\n   - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with payment added\n   - Updates status:\n     - 'paid' when full amount is covered\n     - 'partially_paid' while balance remains\n   - Validates:\n     - Invoice is 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (NOT_ISSUED)\n     - Amount is positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID)\n     - Date is valid YYYY-MM-DD (DATE_INVALID)\n     - Payment doesn't exceed balance (OVERPAYMENT)\n   - Never mutates original invoice\n\n2. **balanceDue(invoice)**\n   - Returns total - sum of payments\n   - Amount still owed on the invoice\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added NOT_ISSUED error code\n- Added OVERPAYMENT error code\n\n**Comprehensive tests covering:**\n- Single and multiple payments\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Full and partial payment scenarios\n- All validation paths (amount, date, status)\n- Overpayment prevention\n- Balance due calculations\n- Immutability (no mutation of originals)\n\n**Example workflow:**\n```\n1. Create invoice (draft)\n2. Issue invoice (status: issued, balance: \u20ac1,452.00)\n3. Record payment \u20ac500 (status: partially_paid, balance: \u20ac952.00)\n4. Record payment \u20ac952 (status: paid, balance: \u20ac0)\n```",
